<title>GERMANY: Bonn orders Telekom to open local network.</title>
<headline>Bonn orders Telekom to open local network.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government on Tuesday ruled in favour of rivals to Deutsche Telekom AG, ordering the phone monopoly to provide an offer to rivals for so-called unbundled interconnection by July 14.</p>
<p>The decision comes as a result of a regulatory complaint by Mannesmann-led Mannesman Arcor, O.Tel.O -- the joint venture of RWE and Veba -- and NetCologne, a city carrier who complained that Telekom was not offering full access for rivals to its local networks.</p>
</text>
